  world-4p-set-1 CPU_OBJECT_RAM DEVICE_OBJECT_RAM
```

The comparison applies the selected machine's active/nonzero-depth
transfer rule, preserving record order and comparing every selected
16-byte record. Inactive payload words may be stale, but every header
after the selected prefix must be zero. Both runs produced:

| Original frame | Selected CPU | Active device | Exact records |
| -------------- | -----------: | ------------: | ------------: |
| 120            | 0            | 0             | 0             |
| 599            | 0            | 0             | 0             |
| 660            | 8            | 8             | 2             |
| 900            | 37           | 37            | 32            |
| 1200           | 0            | 0             | 0             |
| 1500           | 13           | 13            | 4             |

No uncleared headers were observed. The active counts and partial record
agreement corroborate the candidate device buffer's identity; the
different records are preserved as evidence, not treated as exact DMA
equivalence. The CPU and device captures need not reflect the same DMA
instant. All zero-object frames are also the exact background matches.
